course: dictionary
lesson: 9883
title: Taekwondo, a sport from Korea
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Taekwondo is a martial art and sport from Korea. A martial art is a fighting skill that people learn for fitness, self-control and respect. It is famous for high, fast kicks, and for jumping and spinning kicks too.
explain: In a taekwondo class you learn patterns, called forms, and sparring with protective gear. You can also break boards. Children wear a white uniform called a dobok, and coloured belts show their level, up to black belt.
explain: «Judo has been in the Olympics since 1964 and taekwondo since 2000.» The clue is the word Olympics: taekwondo is an Olympic sport, so it is played at the Olympic Games.
explain: Taekwondo is an uncountable noun, so you do not say "a taekwondo". Say "do taekwondo", "taekwondo class" or "black belt in taekwondo". You may also see it written as tae kwon do.
fact: Taekwondo is a martial art and sport from Korea.
fact: Taekwondo is famous for high, fast kicks, and jumping and spinning kicks.
fact: Taekwondo is an Olympic sport, and it has been in the Olympics since 2000.
fact: Children wear a white uniform called a dobok, and coloured belts show their level, up to black belt.
exercise: What country does taekwondo come from? | Brazil | Japan | *Korea | China
exercise: «Judo has been in the Olympics since 1964 and taekwondo since 2000.» In what year did taekwondo join the Olympics? | 2010 | 1964 | 1990 | *2000
exercise: What do children wear for taekwondo? | A swimming costume | A tutu | *A white uniform called a dobok | A school blazer
test: Taekwondo is famous for which kind of move? | Long, slow walking | Slow dancing | Painting pictures | *High, fast kicks
test: Which belt is the top level in taekwondo? | *Black | Green | White | Yellow
exam: Which words finish this sentence correctly? "I do ___ every Tuesday." | a taekwondo | taekwondos | *taekwondo | taekwondoes
